# External GitHub / model integration

**Autonomy (required):** Cursor must **find** relevant GitHub repos itself (web research), pick the best **HTTPS** clone URL (`https://github.com/org/repo.git`), **clone**, and **integrate** — without waiting for the human to paste a link. The human may still paste a link to override or speed things up.

## Discover

1. Search GitHub / the web for repos, models, or libs that match the task.
2. Prefer maintained, well-licensed, focused repos over huge unrelated monorepos.
3. Choose **HTTPS** clone URLs by default (`https://github.com/.../*.git`). Use SSH only if HTTPS fails or the human asks.
4. Record the chosen URL in the summary.

## Clone (do it — don’t only propose)

1. Target: `vendor/<repo-name>` (or a path the human named) — **never** dump into repo root.
2. Run `git clone <https-url> vendor/<repo-name>` yourself.
3. On auth/network failure: report the error; retry HTTPS vs SSH once if sensible; don’t leak credentials.
4. Do **not** commit large weights or full upstream history unless asked. Prefer thin copy, wrap, or document install steps.

## Integrate (do it — don’t stop at clone)

1. Read README + license before wiring.
2. License: MIT/Apache OK to adapt; copyleft / restrictive → warn then pause only if legally blocking.
3. Wire the **smallest useful slice** into RadArt layers (service/collector/feature); wrap upstream, don’t sprawl.
4. Optional deps / feature flags so the demo still runs without the new piece.
5. Afterward: where cloned, URL used, license, what was wired, how to run.

## When the human pastes a link

Use that URL as the source of truth and proceed (clone + integrate) the same way.
